Draw an instance batch before the state it was begun with is changed. Taken from Lichii. A draw.begin
with InstanceId::First then Subsequent pairs is drawn as its first draw at once and as one instanced
draw later; NVN's draw macros reset the base instance and its copy in c[0][0x644] right after the
loop, before the macro returns, so the batch was drawn with base instance 0. OoT's menu text draws
each line's glyphs this way and showed only the first letter of each line. Any register write that
is not part of the loop now draws the waiting instances first.

